1
00:00:00,542 --> 00:00:04,462
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,428 --> 00:00:12,887
[Jepoy] <i>You don't have to</i>
<i>shoulder everything.</i>

3
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:15,223
<i>-We aren't leaving.</i>
<i>-Ana, this is my fight.</i>

4
00:00:15,306 --> 00:00:18,018
<i>You mean our fight. We all want justice.</i>

5
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:20,645
[Ivy] <i>Now that you revealed Ana</i>
<i>as Lily Cruz,</i>

6
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:22,355
<i>I need to rush the wedding!</i>

7
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:27,986
[Emilia] <i>We can join forces</i>
<i>to finally end Lily Cruz.</i>

8
00:00:28,069 --> 00:00:30,113
<i>Julio, I'm sorry. Your cancer is back.</i>

9
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:31,990
[Julio] <i>If I'm going to die,</i>

10
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:34,325
<i>Arnaldo's wedding has to push through.</i>

11
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:38,038
<i>Because he will need Ivy Aguas.</i>

12
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:40,206
[Anna] <i>Why will you marry that monster?</i>

13
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:42,876
[Ivy] <i>Just trust in my plan.</i>

14
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:46,463
<i>Don't try to stop my wedding</i>
<i>or any of my plans.</i>

15
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:49,382
<i>-You're worried I'll lose too.</i>
<i>-Yes!</i>

16
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:52,427
[Julio shouts] <i>Get your act together!</i>

17
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:56,473
<i>Arnaldo, Ardiente is yours for the taking!</i>

18
00:00:56,556 --> 00:00:59,142
<i>Poblacion Ardiente is yours!</i>

19
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:01,519
<i>Grandpa, I promise I won't waste</i>
<i>this second chance you've given me.</i>

20
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:04,147
<i>Make my dream come true, my son.</i>

21
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:07,942
[Ivy] <i>As we talked about earlier,</i>
<i>after my wedding, you need to leave.</i>

22
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:10,320
<i>-But Ivy, you don't--</i>
<i>-We understand, Ivy.</i>

23
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:14,282
[Anna] <i>Just make sure that</i>
<i>Nanny Carlota's killer pays.</i>

24
00:01:14,365 --> 00:01:16,826
[Julio] <i>Let's be close to</i>
<i>each other once again.</i>

25
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:19,746
<i>You need me. I need you.</i>

26
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:22,123
<i>This family needs you.</i>

27
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:24,417
<i>Okay, Papa. What do you want me to do?</i>

28
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:26,628
[Julio] <i>Lily Cruz.</i>

29
00:01:26,711 --> 00:01:28,922
[Camia] <i>Are you sure you're safe, dear?</i>

30
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:32,091
<i>I can't let something bad happen to you.</i>

31
00:01:32,175 --> 00:01:33,760
[Diego] <i>If you're pretending</i>
<i>to be Lily Cruz,</i>

32
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:36,012
<i>you need to learn everything about her.</i>

33
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:36,971
[Jepoy] <i>Wait a minute.</i>

34
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:39,891
<i>You don't want Ivy</i>
<i>to marry Arnaldo either, right?</i>

35
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:41,684
<i>You already know my answer to that.</i>

36
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:47,440
There's no guarantee…

37
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:50,026
that I'll be safe,

38
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:52,195
or that nothing will ever happen to me.

39
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:54,030
But, Mom, I know…

40
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:56,991
you always pray for me.

41
00:01:57,951 --> 00:01:59,077
That's why I know

42
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,497
we're going to win against the Ardientes.

43
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:08,336
Okay, dear.

44
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:13,049
I'm agreeing to all of this now.

45
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,717
[dramatic music playing]

46
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:16,511
But promise me

47
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:19,139
you won't keep any secrets
from me anymore.

48
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:22,058
You have to tell me everything.

49
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,105
Yes, Mom.

50
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:30,608
If that's what you want.

51
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:33,570
Thank you, dear.

52
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,156
Thank you so much.

53
00:02:45,123 --> 00:02:47,167
So, Jaguar is now out of the picture?

54
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:49,294
No, Auntie.

55
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:50,920
Jaguar is the picture.

56
00:02:51,462 --> 00:02:52,297
What?

57
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,507
You expect me to follow what Papa said?

58
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:56,885
That I'll be an obedient daughter

59
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:58,678
doing whatever he wants me to do?

60
00:02:58,761 --> 00:02:59,846
Do you actually believe

61
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:02,515
he'll give the reward
he was talking about?

62
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:04,100
They're all lies, Auntie.

63
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:06,978
That's why I'm still
going to work on Jaguar.

64
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:10,106
Emilia, believe me.

65
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:13,276
Stay with Julio. Go for the familiar evil.

66
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:16,112
The thing is, Aunt Claire,

67
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:19,407
I feel different for this Jaguar.

68
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:21,284
This is something new.

69
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,620
I have this feeling
that he'll take care of me.

70
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:26,331
Or he'll take you to hell!

71
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:27,832
Oh, that's exciting then!

72
00:03:29,542 --> 00:03:31,544
Emilia, tell me.

73
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,212
Do you like Jaguar?

74
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,425
Aunt Claire, I'm just a woman.

75
00:03:37,508 --> 00:03:39,344
-I have weaknesses too.
-Oh my goodness.

76
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:43,473
You know, I crave
for a powerful man's attention,

77
00:03:43,556 --> 00:03:46,100
which I'm getting from Jaguar right now.

78
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:47,685
So, can you blame me?

79
00:03:48,353 --> 00:03:49,729
You're too old for this, Emilia.

80
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:52,482
-Please.
-Oh no, Auntie.

81
00:03:52,565 --> 00:03:55,443
Being desired doesn't stop
until you're 70.

82
00:03:55,526 --> 00:03:57,028
Now you know!

83
00:03:57,111 --> 00:04:02,033
So if I have to use my body

84
00:04:02,116 --> 00:04:04,661
to get that Jaguar,

85
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:06,120
I'll do it, Auntie.

86
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:09,457
-Emilia, you're crazy.
-[Emilia laughs]

87
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,292
Auntie, that's obvious.

88
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:12,877
And stubborn.

89
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:21,761
Anna.

90
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:24,764
If you're going to pretend to be Lily,

91
00:04:24,847 --> 00:04:26,182
I have one condition.

92
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:30,478
Like what we discussed,

93
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:32,355
on the day of my wedding,
you need to leave.

94
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:34,440
I've already booked your tickets.

95
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,609
And called my secretary.

96
00:04:37,485 --> 00:04:39,737
-But Ivy, you don't--
-We understand, Ivy.

97
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:43,408
-We'll leave on that day.
-[tense music playing]

98
00:04:43,491 --> 00:04:47,787
Just make sure the man who
killed Nanny Carlota will pay.

99
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:51,499
[Camia] So--

100
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:57,088
Batch.

101
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:58,172
Hey, Batch.

102
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:00,508
[Marlon] Good thing you're back.

103
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:02,844
It looks like we have a visitor.

104
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:05,430
Batch, call everyone.

105
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:07,307
Miss Loring, Mister Pandoy.

106
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,517
Everyone, Diego's here.

107
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,853
Can everyone just gather around, please?

108
00:05:11,936 --> 00:05:13,563
-Come on.
-Nanny, Uncle.

109
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:32,582
Of course, you already know Jepoy.

110
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,751
Good evening.

111
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:35,752
But…

112
00:05:36,544 --> 00:05:39,338
…there's someone Aunt Camia
and I would like you to meet.

113
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:41,591
Friends…

114
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,469
she's finally back in Ardiente.

115
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:47,513
My daughter, Lily Cruz.

116
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:50,141
-Did you say Lily Cruz?
-Lily?

117
00:05:50,224 --> 00:05:52,393
[Loring giggles]

118
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:54,479
Is that you, Lily?

119
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:55,730
-Yes, it's me.
-Oh my!

120
00:05:57,398 --> 00:05:58,608
[Loring] Oh my goodness!

121
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:03,404
[pensive music playing]

122
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:15,958
Thank goodness, you're back.

123
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:20,588
I've wanted to come back
to Ardiente for so long.

124
00:06:20,963 --> 00:06:22,632
I missed you all!

125
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:27,136
[Loring] We missed you too.

126
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,638
[Loring giggles]

127
00:06:28,721 --> 00:06:30,848
Oh my goodness!

128
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:32,725
I can't believe it!

129
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:34,560
Wait, don't you miss someone else?

130
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:39,649
What about your best friend here?

131
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:40,650
[laughing]

132
00:06:42,985 --> 00:06:44,570
-Nanny, stop it.
-[Ana giggles]

133
00:06:44,904 --> 00:06:47,657
Of course, I missed Diego too.

134
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:53,621
Let's go.

135
00:06:59,710 --> 00:07:02,046
-I thought so too!
-[Pandoy chuckles]

136
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:07,718
-[Ana and Loring giggle]
-Umm…

137
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:12,223
And of course, we're even stronger now

138
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:13,599
because my best friend is here.

139
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:16,936
She'll help in our campaign.

140
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,730
-Wow!
-Thank you.

141
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,649
I'm so glad that you're back.

142
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:23,234
You know…

143
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:26,362
We've been looking for you for so long.

144
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:27,697
Yeah, Diego's been waiting for you.

145
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:30,741
Let's just go inside and talk there.

146
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:33,494
-Diego's been looking for you.
-Come in.

147
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:35,580
-[Ana laughs]
-Come in.

148
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:38,583
-[Pandoy] Congratulations!
-[Camia] Thank you, Uncle.

149
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:46,716
You know, I finished
all my transactions in Manila

150
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:50,303
just because I couldn't let a day pass

151
00:07:50,386 --> 00:07:52,221
without seeing you, hon.

152
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:55,057
If you ask me, I think
I'm going crazy over you.

153
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:56,601
[Arnaldo chuckles]

154
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:59,604
-Me too, hon.
-Really?

155
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:03,399
Hon, what if we speed up our wedding?

156
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:05,943
Why not do it next week?

157
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:07,236
What do you think?

158
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,113
Well, as much as I want to,

159
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:12,033
Grandpa and I agreed

160
00:08:12,116 --> 00:08:14,035
that we have to take care
of Lily Cruz first.

161
00:08:16,329 --> 00:08:17,955
-Oh.
-[tense music playing]

162
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:20,750
Why? Are you guys planning to…

163
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:23,878
silence Lily Cruz?

164
00:08:23,961 --> 00:08:27,507
Unfortunately, everyone
who goes against our family

165
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,592
has to learn one way or another.

166
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:34,222
Lily Cruz.

167
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:37,892
Hon, is now the best time for that?

168
00:08:38,309 --> 00:08:41,604
If you kill Lily Cruz,
who will people blame?

169
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:42,772
You.

170
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:44,482
"Arnaldo killed Lily Cruz."

171
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,901
"He's a murderer. He needs to be in jail."

172
00:08:46,984 --> 00:08:49,153
"He doesn't deserve to be the governor."

173
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:52,198
Hon, do you get what I'm saying?

174
00:08:52,698 --> 00:08:53,658
I get it.

175
00:08:53,741 --> 00:08:55,576
I already thought of that, but…

176
00:08:56,369 --> 00:08:57,912
I don't call the shots anymore.

177
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:00,248
Grandpa does, and I trust him.

178
00:09:03,042 --> 00:09:04,085
But…

179
00:09:04,168 --> 00:09:06,587
what if we talk to your grandfather?

180
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:11,551
You know, hon, Lily Cruz isn't a problem.

181
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:16,389
Actually, I think that Lily Cruz…

182
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:19,600
can be…

183
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:23,604
the solution to all your problems.

184
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:26,649
The solution?

185
00:09:28,025 --> 00:09:28,901
How?

186
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,238
Hon.

187
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:34,532
Just trust me on this.

188
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:37,493
You need to support me on this.

189
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,287
Because I'm sure that

190
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:41,497
whatever I say to your grandfather,

191
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:45,376
I bet your mother will oppose as usual.

192
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:48,004
All right. Tell me what you need.

193
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:51,382
Later.

194
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:52,592
Hug me first.

195
00:09:54,552 --> 00:09:55,595
[Arnaldo] I missed you.

196
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,598
I missed you so much, hon.

197
00:10:01,183 --> 00:10:03,185
[tense music playing]

198
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:05,855
[Ivy] <i>Why?</i>

199
00:10:05,938 --> 00:10:09,775
<i>Are you guys planning</i>
<i>to silence Lily Cruz?</i>

200
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:13,487
<i>Unfortunately, everyone</i>
<i>who goes against our family</i>

201
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:15,406
<i>has to learn one way or another.</i>

202
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:19,619
How many times will you have me killed?

203
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:22,496
The people I love

204
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,498
are always on your list of targets.

205
00:10:24,582 --> 00:10:26,667
My father, my mother,

206
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:30,379
Nanny Carlota, Diego, and Jepoy.

207
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:33,007
And now, you want Anna killed.

208
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:40,723
I am the real Lily Cruz.

209
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:45,353
The one who'll drag you all to hell.

210
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:48,230
Because that's what you deserve.

211
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:52,985
-I'm the real Lily Cruz!
-[tense music intensifies]

212
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:56,739
[indistinct chatter]

213
00:10:58,199 --> 00:11:00,576
-Here, have some coffee.
-Thank you.

214
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:09,669
[Camia sighs]

215
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:10,586
Anna.

216
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:15,216
I want to apologize in advance.

217
00:11:16,675 --> 00:11:19,970
I just find it hard to trust people.

218
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,764
[soft piano music playing]

219
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:24,350
I was deceived by Nimfa in the past.

220
00:11:26,143 --> 00:11:28,979
She got close to me
and betrayed me in the end.

221
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:32,983
I'd never do that, Miss Camia.

222
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:35,569
Ivy is my friend.

223
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:41,158
But I understand how you feel.

224
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:44,954
There's only one Lily in your heart,

225
00:11:46,288 --> 00:11:47,790
and that's Ivy.

226
00:11:57,716 --> 00:11:59,802
DIEGO FOR THE NEW ARDIENTE

227
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:01,720
Here are the records.

228
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:04,890
Mr. Diego is here.

229
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:07,184
Arnaldo is desperate.

230
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:08,644
-What happened?
-Why?

231
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:10,229
He's handing this out to everyone.

232
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:15,651
He's giving away money and rice.

233
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:16,610
It isn't right.

234
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:20,072
-Let me see. Wow, some rice.
-Is it fresh?

235
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:23,492
There's an envelope here too.

236
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:24,493
[Loring] Let me see.

237
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:26,454
[Pandoy laughs]

238
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:29,248
See what I mean?
He's using money to get votes.

239
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:31,834
Well, at least it's just rice and money.

240
00:12:31,917 --> 00:12:35,796
I mean, if he uses bullets,
we're in trouble.

241
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:39,175
-[Loring] Yes.
-They could resort to violence.

242
00:12:39,925 --> 00:12:41,135
He's so desperate.

243
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:42,845
-I can buy sardines with this.
-Come in.

244
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:46,223
Batch, they're my friends
from Ardiente News Network.

245
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:48,601
They want to interview you and Lily Cruz.

246
00:12:49,351 --> 00:12:51,353
The Ardientes won't see this coming.

247
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:53,689
Lily's on her way here too, right?

248
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:54,982
Let's include her.

249
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:56,859
-Batch, come here.
-What?

250
00:12:56,942 --> 00:12:59,028
Can we please leave Lily out of this?

251
00:12:59,111 --> 00:12:59,904
Why?

252
00:12:59,987 --> 00:13:02,156
I don't want her to be
a target of the Ardientes.

253
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:03,741
[ominous music playing]

254
00:13:03,824 --> 00:13:05,493
Okay. I'll tell them.

255
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:07,077
-I'm sorry.
-Thank you.

256
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:10,748
I'm sorry but they're not ready.

257
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:12,416
Let's just do it next week. I'll call you.

258
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,626
-Okay.
-Thank you.

259
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:15,503
-I'm sorry.
-We'll reschedule.

260
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:16,837
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

261
00:13:16,921 --> 00:13:18,214
Thank you.

262
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:24,762
[ominous music intensifies]

263
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:32,645
Give me one.

264
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:40,486
[cell phone ringing]

265
00:13:43,572 --> 00:13:44,698
I'm in position.

266
00:13:59,004 --> 00:14:00,673
So, Ivy, how do you find the food?

267
00:14:00,756 --> 00:14:01,882
You want more?

268
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:04,635
I can ask the maid to prepare more.

269
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:07,596
Or maybe, I suggest salad,

270
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:11,433
since you're preparing for
the big day, your wedding day.

271
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,561
Thank you, Emilia. You're so sweet.

272
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:14,603
[Ivy] I'm fine, thank you.

273
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:16,063
[Emilia] You're most welcome.

274
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:22,611
You know, Ivy, I am so happy

275
00:14:22,695 --> 00:14:25,656
the animosity between us is finally over.

276
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:27,616
I feel so relieved.

277
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,493
You know, if we weren't eating,

278
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:31,287
I could've hugged you right now.

279
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:32,872
Well, me too.

280
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:36,125
It actually annoyed me
when all these doubts

281
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:38,252
and allegations were thrown against me.

282
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:40,421
[Ivy] So finally, you're enlightened.

283
00:14:41,797 --> 00:14:42,798
Yeah.

284
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:45,301
I'm so happy that

285
00:14:45,384 --> 00:14:48,512
we can be best friends again, like before.

286
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:52,683
Actually, we can be like sisters.

287
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:54,226
Can I call you Sis?

288
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:56,478
[Ivy and Julio laugh]

289
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:57,730
Emilia!

290
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:00,232
Emilia's cracking jokes again.

291
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:01,692
-"Sis"?
-Yeah.

292
00:15:01,775 --> 00:15:04,486
[Ivy] But we've got a huge age gap.

293
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:07,740
I'm okay with calling you
my "future mother-in-law".

294
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:10,576
After my wedding to Arnaldo,

295
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:14,496
you can decide
what you'd like to be called.

296
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:17,166
I can call you "Ma," "Mom," or "Mama."

297
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:20,502
[Ivy] That's more fitting, I guess.

298
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:21,962
What do you think?

299
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:26,759
Pardon me for butting in, but…

300
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:29,678
Ivy is right, Emilia.

301
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,555
And I believe,

302
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:37,269
among the choices,
"Mama" would fit you just right.

303
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:40,856
-Right.
-It sounds more regal, right?

304
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,316
Yes! "Mama".

305
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:43,442
-You see?
-Mama Emilia.

306
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:45,235
-Mama Emilia.
-Yeah!

307
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:47,696
Mama Emilia.

308
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:48,864
[tense music playing]

309
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:49,865
And…

310
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,494
…the truth of the matter is,
I'm very happy that, finally,

311
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:55,663
both of you have decided

312
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:58,499
to bury the proverbial hatchet.

313
00:15:58,582 --> 00:15:59,500
Um-hm.

314
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:01,710
[Ivy] Yes, Congressman. I'm so happy.

315
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:05,714
Emilia's great at burying things.

316
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:07,633
-What?
-[Emilia coughs]

317
00:16:07,716 --> 00:16:08,550
She's good at burying…

318
00:16:09,718 --> 00:16:11,595
resentment.

319
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:14,723
Oh, yeah.

320
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:17,935
Speaking of burying.

321
00:16:18,852 --> 00:16:20,688
I want you to witness…

322
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:24,483
Lily Cruz being buried alive.

323
00:16:24,566 --> 00:16:26,568
[ominous music playing]

324
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:30,280
I'm sure you're going to do that for us.

325
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:35,619
We're family now.

326
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:38,288
[ominous music intensifies]

327
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:41,750
[tense music playing]

328
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,492
Of course.

329
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:17,703
Now that I'm marrying Arnaldo…

330
00:17:17,786 --> 00:17:20,330
-I'm going to be an Ardiente.
-[ominous music playing]

331
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:22,541
It's so exciting.

332
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:26,211
When exactly are you
going to get Lily Cruz?

333
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,005
-I can't wait.
-[Emilia giggles]

334
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:29,381
I love it. Perfect.

335
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:30,591
This is just so exciting.

336
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:33,218
In fact, I'm going to make
a phone call right now.

337
00:17:33,594 --> 00:17:36,430
So, are you all ready to witness

338
00:17:36,513 --> 00:17:39,725
the fall of Lily Cruz…

339
00:17:41,977 --> 00:17:43,187
and Madrigal?

340
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:47,191
Because it's just one call away.

341
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:49,318
I just need to dial it.

342
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:50,694
Are you all ready?

343
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,155
[ominous music intensifies]

344
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:13,258
Could you just excuse me, please?

345
00:18:15,052 --> 00:18:17,429
[tense music playing]

346
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,689
-Auntie.
-Hello, Diego.

347
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:31,068
[henchman cocks gun]

348
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:33,487
-Diego.
-You're here.

349
00:18:33,570 --> 00:18:36,615
Of course, we need
to do well in our campaign.

350
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,788
[henchman cocks gun]

351
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:48,377
[tense music intensifies]

352
00:18:54,716 --> 00:18:58,595
Hon, I guess we should tell
your grandfather about our plan.

353
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:01,598
Congressman, I have a proposal.

354
00:19:02,057 --> 00:19:03,392
A proposal?

355
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:06,395
Have the posters arrived?

356
00:19:06,478 --> 00:19:08,564
[Diego] Yes, Auntie.
The first batch came in.

357
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:09,940
[Camia] That's good.

358
00:19:10,023 --> 00:19:12,025
[Diego] I'll ask Marlon to do
a follow-up, so?

359
00:19:12,109 --> 00:19:13,443
[Camia] So we can start distributing them.

360
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:14,570
[Diego] You're right.

361
00:19:14,653 --> 00:19:18,365
Lily Cruz is the public's symbol of hope.

362
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:21,577
The girl who lived
after Emilia ordered her killed.

363
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:26,623
Well, if you want to have
Lily Cruz and Madrigal killed,

364
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:29,042
who do you think
the public will blame again?

365
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:30,961
The Ardientes.

366
00:19:31,044 --> 00:19:32,629
They'll point their
fingers at Arnaldo again.

367
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:36,592
We'd be committing
political suicide if we do that.

368
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:42,014
Yes. We started discussing
our plans for this Sunday.

369
00:19:43,348 --> 00:19:46,268
So Congressman, Arnaldo and I figured,

370
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:48,478
maybe we should postpone the assassination

371
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:50,480
of Lily Cruz and Madrigal.

372
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:53,150
Instead, we offer a peace treaty.

373
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:54,401
A cease-fire.

374
00:19:54,484 --> 00:19:56,028
A publicity stunt.

375
00:19:56,111 --> 00:19:59,114
We have to make Arnaldo look good.

376
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,490
That's what he needs right now.

377
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:04,119
A good image to please
the public and the press.

378
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:06,496
Congressman, we'll give them freedom.

379
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:10,667
But the reality is,
it'll all just be an illusion.

380
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:11,960
[cell phone ringing]

381
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:13,420
Hello, boss?

382
00:20:13,503 --> 00:20:16,840
Make it fast and make it quick, okay?

383
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:20,052
I don't want any survivors.

384
00:20:20,135 --> 00:20:21,220
Do you hear me?

385
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:22,679
Yes, boss.

386
00:20:22,763 --> 00:20:25,224
-All right, bye.
-What do you think, Congressman?

387
00:20:25,307 --> 00:20:26,892
I have a point, right?

388
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:28,977
[clears throat]

389
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:35,150
[henchman cocks gun]

390
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:38,570
[tense music intensifies]

391
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:44,743
Hon?

392
00:20:45,577 --> 00:20:46,662
What do you think?

393
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:49,581
It's all for you. It's all for Arnaldo.

394
00:21:06,306 --> 00:21:07,391
Emilia.

395
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:09,977
Stop the operation.

396
00:21:10,727 --> 00:21:14,273
But I just made the phone call
and it's all set.

397
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:21,280
I said stop the operation.

398
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:23,490
Papa, I already told our men
to proceed with--

399
00:21:23,573 --> 00:21:25,575
Stop it now!

400
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:28,120
Can't you hear me?!
You got wax in your ears?!

401
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:30,414
Make the call.

402
00:21:31,581 --> 00:21:32,958
-Now?
-Now!

403
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:34,835
I will, okay? Now.

404
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:41,717
[cell phone ringing]

405
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:44,553
Boss?

406
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:46,138
Abort.

407
00:21:46,221 --> 00:21:47,431
Yes, boss.

408
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:48,682
Abort.

409
00:21:48,765 --> 00:21:49,766
Let's go!

410
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:56,106
[Diego] Let's start in the smaller areas.

411
00:21:56,189 --> 00:21:59,526
[Camia] Right, all the
outlying neighborhoods.

412
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:05,073
-Auntie Camia.
-What?

413
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:06,742
We have to go inside.

414
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:08,243
Is there something wrong, Jepoy?

415
00:22:08,618 --> 00:22:10,537
We'll be much safer inside.

416
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:11,496
Let's go.

417
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,790
-Jepoy is right.
-All right then.

418
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:30,599
It's all for you, hon.

419
00:22:35,562 --> 00:22:37,522
Get ready, Emilia.

420
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:41,443
You, Arnaldo, and Ivy are going somewhere.

421
00:22:54,289 --> 00:22:55,332
[indistinct chatter]

422
00:23:04,299 --> 00:23:05,383
Everyone, listen up!

423
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:07,677
-The Ardientes are here.
-[tense music playing]

424
00:23:22,150 --> 00:23:23,026
[Emilia sighs]

425
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:27,906
[slow tense music playing]

426
00:23:28,573 --> 00:23:29,616
[Emilia] Oh!

427
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:32,577
Good morning!

428
00:23:34,496 --> 00:23:36,414
It's indeed a good morning.

429
00:23:36,957 --> 00:23:38,583
[Emilia] Wow!

430
00:23:40,001 --> 00:23:41,753
Is that Lily Cruz…

431
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,798
Madrigal…

432
00:23:45,757 --> 00:23:48,176
…Diego and Camia Cruz?

433
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:50,428
Too bad, I didn't bring my checklist,

434
00:23:50,512 --> 00:23:52,305
because you would've gotten
a perfect attendance!

435
00:23:53,598 --> 00:23:54,808
Wait.

436
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:58,812
So, this is where you make your plans.

437
00:23:58,895 --> 00:24:01,773
But I see your HQ isn't finished yet.

438
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:03,024
The place still needs work.

439
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:04,442
Not enough money?

440
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:06,486
No worries, it works for you.

441
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:07,737
It looks so cheap.

442
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:08,989
[Emilia giggles]

443
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:11,116
What are you doing here, Emilia?

444
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:16,288
If you think we don't know
what you're up to, you're wrong.

445
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:19,624
Isn't it enough
that you sent your men here,

446
00:24:19,708 --> 00:24:22,544
that you had to personally come
and scare us?

447
00:24:22,627 --> 00:24:25,630
Camia, why are you so livid?

448
00:24:25,714 --> 00:24:26,965
You're in such a bad mood.

449
00:24:27,048 --> 00:24:30,010
You should actually be glad
that I didn't kill you.

450
00:24:30,093 --> 00:24:31,553
You should thank me.

451
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:35,015
We don't trust any of you Ardientes.

452
00:24:35,974 --> 00:24:37,100
Camia.

453
00:24:37,767 --> 00:24:39,603
Why are you becoming such a war freak?

454
00:24:39,686 --> 00:24:41,354
It clashes with your outfit.

455
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:43,773
You look so pure today.

456
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:46,484
I came here for peace and harmony.

457
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:47,485
[Camia laughs]

458
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:49,529
-Harmony?!
-Yeah.

459
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:52,782
What do you Ardientes know
about peace and harmony?

460
00:24:53,366 --> 00:24:54,242
Camia.

461
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:58,538
The Ardientes aren't as bad as you think.

462
00:24:59,581 --> 00:25:01,333
Yes, this is the proof.

463
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:06,004
This is a peace agreement.

464
00:25:07,464 --> 00:25:09,341
From this day on,

465
00:25:09,424 --> 00:25:13,678
the killing, cheating, and blackmailing

466
00:25:13,762 --> 00:25:15,722
between Diego Torillo

467
00:25:15,805 --> 00:25:18,016
and Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo will stop.

468
00:25:18,725 --> 00:25:20,685
If you agree to it, Diego,

469
00:25:20,769 --> 00:25:22,896
we're going to hold a press conference.

470
00:25:23,563 --> 00:25:25,398
And we expect you to attend.

471
00:25:29,903 --> 00:25:30,946
Diego?

472
00:25:32,697 --> 00:25:35,617
[tense music intensifies]

473
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,602
What are you waiting for? A drum roll?

474
00:26:02,686 --> 00:26:03,728
Just take it.

475
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:05,689
Hon.

476
00:26:08,817 --> 00:26:09,859
[Ivy] Hon.

477
00:26:09,943 --> 00:26:11,486
He's the only one in a bad mood today.

478
00:26:11,569 --> 00:26:12,696
I'm in a good mood.

479
00:26:12,779 --> 00:26:14,489
Bye, thanks.

480
00:26:14,572 --> 00:26:15,323
See you!

481
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:16,866
Start the car.

482
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:42,809
Hon.

483
00:26:42,892 --> 00:26:44,144
-Come here.
-Arnaldo.

484
00:26:45,312 --> 00:26:47,272
Ouch! You're hurting me!

485
00:26:47,355 --> 00:26:48,565
Hon, stop it!

486
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:51,818
Arnaldo!

487
00:26:51,901 --> 00:26:53,403
Do you want someone else to kiss you?!

488
00:26:54,446 --> 00:26:55,488
Hon.

489
00:26:56,072 --> 00:26:57,324
You know, I just realized that

490
00:26:57,407 --> 00:26:59,034
with this cease-fire going on,

491
00:26:59,909 --> 00:27:02,579
you and Diego will have more
opportunities to grow closer.

492
00:27:03,705 --> 00:27:04,998
I'm right, aren't I?

493
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:07,751
Hon, seriously?

494
00:27:07,834 --> 00:27:09,002
Everything I'm doing,

495
00:27:09,085 --> 00:27:10,795
the press conference, the peace agreement,

496
00:27:10,879 --> 00:27:12,505
this is all for you!

497
00:27:12,589 --> 00:27:14,883
Because I want to save your reputation.

498
00:27:15,383 --> 00:27:17,802
I'm doing all this for you!

499
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:19,763
Because I'm all yours, Arnaldo!

500
00:27:19,846 --> 00:27:21,681
When will you believe me?!

501
00:27:27,896 --> 00:27:28,938
[sighs]

502
00:27:29,564 --> 00:27:30,565
Okay.

503
00:27:31,608 --> 00:27:33,401
I know you're jealous again.

504
00:27:39,074 --> 00:27:40,158
Hon.

505
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:43,870
I'll make it up to you.

506
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:46,081
Come on.

507
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:49,501
Let's go.

508
00:27:49,584 --> 00:27:50,919
I'll make it up to you.

509
00:27:51,002 --> 00:27:52,128
You want me to, right?

510
00:27:55,757 --> 00:27:56,883
Good grief!

511
00:27:56,966 --> 00:28:01,513
What are those Ardientes up to this time?

512
00:28:01,596 --> 00:28:06,518
Diego, I'll ask volunteers to
watch over our headquarters,

513
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:09,270
so the Ardientes won't
come back here ever again!

514
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:10,397
You're right, Mr. Pandoy.

515
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:12,982
We need to tighten
the security around here.

516
00:28:13,525 --> 00:28:16,569
[Loring] Exactly. Right, Diego?

517
00:28:18,738 --> 00:28:19,864
Diego?

518
00:28:19,948 --> 00:28:21,116
Hey, Diego.

519
00:28:21,616 --> 00:28:23,493
Are you listening?

520
00:28:26,287 --> 00:28:30,375
Diego, don't tell me
you believe everything

521
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:32,627
that Ivy and the Ardientes said?

522
00:28:32,710 --> 00:28:34,587
I mean, a press conference?

523
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:37,590
Miss Loring, Diego needs to attend.

524
00:28:38,341 --> 00:28:40,927
If he doesn't, it'll reflect badly on him.

525
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:42,887
My goodness. But…

526
00:28:44,597 --> 00:28:45,598
He's right, Nanny.

527
00:28:46,349 --> 00:28:47,934
[Loring] All right then.

528
00:28:48,393 --> 00:28:52,605
For now, I'll just
prepare something to eat.

529
00:28:53,273 --> 00:28:55,859
Let me help you with that.

530
00:28:56,151 --> 00:28:57,694
I'll help you too.

531
00:28:57,777 --> 00:28:59,028
All right.

532
00:29:03,992 --> 00:29:04,993
Diego.

533
00:29:05,702 --> 00:29:07,328
What's your plan now?

534
00:29:08,955 --> 00:29:10,290
I'll go there.

535
00:29:11,249 --> 00:29:12,292
We all will.

536
00:29:12,375 --> 00:29:14,586
We'll make peace with the Ardientes.

537
00:29:15,253 --> 00:29:18,298
What if that peace treaty is just a sham?

538
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:21,092
There must be a reason why Ivy came here.

539
00:29:21,634 --> 00:29:25,805
I'm sure she planned all this
for everyone's sake.

540
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:29,601
[suspenseful music playing]

541
00:29:33,563 --> 00:29:35,482
[Emilia] If Ivy didn't
interfere with our plan,

542
00:29:35,565 --> 00:29:37,901
Lily Cruz would've been gone by now.

543
00:29:38,985 --> 00:29:41,196
Emilia, you're mad at Ivy again.

544
00:29:41,654 --> 00:29:43,615
I thought you buried the hatchet?

545
00:29:43,698 --> 00:29:45,533
Especially since the
peace treaty with Diego's camp

546
00:29:45,617 --> 00:29:46,868
was all her idea.

547
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:48,703
It's not just that, Auntie.

548
00:29:49,287 --> 00:29:51,706
You know why I'm so irritated now?

549
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:53,416
Because Papa sided with her.

550
00:29:54,292 --> 00:29:57,587
I swear Auntie, you're the only
one I trust in this family.

551
00:29:58,671 --> 00:29:59,631
Of course.

552
00:30:00,381 --> 00:30:02,592
Don't worry, I'll always be here for you.

553
00:30:03,301 --> 00:30:05,136
Thank you, Auntie. But you know what?

554
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:07,388
This press conference
is actually good for me.

555
00:30:07,472 --> 00:30:10,266
Because I'll have the opportunity

556
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:15,021
to see what that Lily Cruz is up to.

557
00:30:15,438 --> 00:30:17,482
Who knows? I might
find a way to bring her,

558
00:30:17,565 --> 00:30:19,609
and Diego down in that event.

559
00:30:20,527 --> 00:30:22,862
We just decided to have a peace agreement,

560
00:30:22,946 --> 00:30:26,324
yet here you are,
with another vicious plan.

561
00:30:27,283 --> 00:30:29,118
Ms. Claire, what's with Emilia?

562
00:30:30,578 --> 00:30:33,665
Whatever your plan is, please stop it.

563
00:30:33,748 --> 00:30:35,500
You'll just cause trouble.

564
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:38,044
Ivy, wait.

565
00:30:38,127 --> 00:30:41,631
Let me just remind you
about the promise you made.

566
00:30:41,714 --> 00:30:43,258
You told me:

567
00:30:43,341 --> 00:30:47,846
"Don't worry, my future mother-in-law."

568
00:30:48,263 --> 00:30:51,558
"We will bring down
that Lily Cruz together."

569
00:30:51,641 --> 00:30:53,518
What happened now?
Did you just change your mind?

570
00:30:54,310 --> 00:30:57,605
Don't tell me you're starting
to like that Lily Cruz?

571
00:30:57,689 --> 00:31:00,441
Just like how you feel
something special for Diego.

572
00:31:00,525 --> 00:31:02,151
[giggles]

573
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:04,028
Emilia, a promise is a promise.

574
00:31:04,362 --> 00:31:06,531
You know what?
I have a new nickname for you.

575
00:31:06,614 --> 00:31:09,993
Emilia "Paranoid" Ardiente-Torillo.

576
00:31:10,076 --> 00:31:11,786
Want to know why you're paranoid?

577
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:13,037
Because of this!

578
00:31:13,121 --> 00:31:15,498
Why don't you try wearing
one necklace at a time?

579
00:31:15,582 --> 00:31:18,084
I promise you, this press conference

580
00:31:18,167 --> 00:31:22,547
is for Arnaldo and for us, Ardientes.

581
00:31:23,172 --> 00:31:24,257
See?

582
00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:25,508
We aren't married yet,

583
00:31:25,592 --> 00:31:28,928
but I already consider myself an Ardiente.

584
00:31:30,305 --> 00:31:31,598
After the press conference,

585
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:35,602
then you can do whatever
you want with Lily Cruz.

586
00:31:37,103 --> 00:31:38,771
And you'll be helping me.

587
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:40,940
Yes.

588
00:31:41,774 --> 00:31:42,775
Okay.

589
00:31:48,698 --> 00:31:49,616
Hello, Rufo.

590
00:31:51,451 --> 00:31:53,578
Diego and Arnaldo will be
holding a press conference.

591
00:31:54,287 --> 00:31:55,747
I need you to do something.

592
00:31:58,082 --> 00:32:00,376
-[Anna] Have another sandwich.
-Thank you.

593
00:32:00,460 --> 00:32:03,504
-This is so good!
-Yes, here, have some more.

594
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:05,506
-Even back in high school?
-Don't be shy.

595
00:32:05,590 --> 00:32:06,966
-Where are we going later?
-Where'd you get this?

596
00:32:07,050 --> 00:32:09,510
Sandwich, sir?
I know you already got three…

597
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:11,512
-…but that's not enough.
-I made that!

598
00:32:11,596 --> 00:32:13,765
-It's tiring.
-I know.

599
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:15,683
[Anna giggles] Okay.

600
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:17,393
[Loring] Look at them.

601
00:32:17,477 --> 00:32:18,811
-Original recipe.
-Have another sandwich.

602
00:32:18,895 --> 00:32:20,480
-Thanks!
-Lily.

603
00:32:20,563 --> 00:32:23,733
You've been serving us all day.

604
00:32:23,816 --> 00:32:26,611
-Why don't you join us?
-Sit down, let's eat.

605
00:32:26,694 --> 00:32:28,696
-It's fine, Mom. I'm still full.
-Yeah, join us.

606
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:30,657
[Anna] Let me know when you're done.

607
00:32:30,740 --> 00:32:32,533
-I'll take those to the kitchen.
-All right.

608
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:34,494
Let us handle it, Lily.

609
00:32:34,577 --> 00:32:38,206
You still have to go to
the press conference with Diego.

610
00:32:38,289 --> 00:32:40,500
It's fine, Mr. Pandoy. This isn't much.

611
00:32:40,583 --> 00:32:44,712
Lily's always been so
hardworking, even as a kid.

612
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:47,048
She always helped her parents out too,

613
00:32:47,131 --> 00:32:51,260
and now she's even better
at helping out the townspeople.

614
00:32:52,345 --> 00:32:53,680
You really are something, Lily.

615
00:32:53,763 --> 00:32:54,722
He's right.

616
00:32:59,936 --> 00:33:01,604
You're right, Nanny.

617
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:03,564
My best friend hasn't changed.

618
00:33:04,315 --> 00:33:07,819
Besides, remember she helped me
lose weight when I was a kid?

619
00:33:07,986 --> 00:33:10,029
-Yeah.
-[laughs]

620
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:11,364
-Diego.
-Hey, Batch.

621
00:33:11,447 --> 00:33:13,116
This could be the start of something new.

622
00:33:13,199 --> 00:33:15,660
-Wait, that sounds like--
-Keep it professional, Batch.

623
00:33:15,743 --> 00:33:17,036
Watch what you're saying, Marlon.

624
00:33:17,120 --> 00:33:19,580
They're just picking up
where they left off.

625
00:33:19,664 --> 00:33:21,874
Really? Well, Miss Loring,

626
00:33:21,958 --> 00:33:25,628
Mister Pandoy, this is how
you form strong bonds.

627
00:33:25,712 --> 00:33:27,088
With a little…

628
00:33:29,424 --> 00:33:31,050
-Marlon.
-Her mom's here.

629
00:33:31,134 --> 00:33:33,136
-Marlon, I'm right here.
-Ms. Camia.

630
00:33:33,219 --> 00:33:35,972
Don't worry, Ma'am.
I was just kidding around.

631
00:33:36,055 --> 00:33:38,850
[Camia] Just finish your
sandwich. Come on, eat up.

632
00:33:38,933 --> 00:33:41,894
[Marlon] I'll just have some
coffee. And keep quiet.

633
00:33:46,816 --> 00:33:49,193
[reporter] Today, we'll witness
the Torillo brothers

634
00:33:49,277 --> 00:33:52,238
signing a peace agreement,
which will start a cease-fire

635
00:33:52,321 --> 00:33:54,657
between the two parties
for a peaceful election.

636
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:59,162
[tense music playing]

637
00:34:27,690 --> 00:34:28,775
Thank you.

638
00:34:51,255 --> 00:34:53,841
[crowd applauds]

639
00:35:07,772 --> 00:35:09,732
[tense music continues playing]

640
00:35:33,756 --> 00:35:34,966
Viva Ardiente.

641
00:35:38,636 --> 00:35:39,971
[man] Everyone, please be seated.

642
00:35:40,054 --> 00:35:42,515
You may now ask
the candidates your questions.

643
00:35:42,598 --> 00:35:43,558
Thank you.

644
00:35:44,183 --> 00:35:46,394
My question is for Mayor Arnaldo Torillo.

645
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:51,190
Why did you decide to agree to
a cease-fire with Diego Torillo?

646
00:35:53,067 --> 00:35:55,111
Well, as you already know,

647
00:35:55,194 --> 00:35:58,030
this campaign period
is turning into a circus.

648
00:35:58,573 --> 00:36:01,701
There have been so many deaths
and a lot of accusations.

649
00:36:01,784 --> 00:36:04,745
We all condemn those killings.

650
00:36:04,829 --> 00:36:09,500
So, my beloved brother and I
decided to call it a truce

651
00:36:09,584 --> 00:36:12,795
for the sake of the citizens
of Poblacion Ardiente.

652
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:15,089
[crowd applauds]

653
00:36:25,141 --> 00:36:27,059
[man] Viva Ardiente!

654
00:36:31,647 --> 00:36:33,065
Mr. Diego Torillo,

655
00:36:33,149 --> 00:36:35,568
why did you agree
to the said peace agreement?

656
00:36:41,574 --> 00:36:45,077
The safety of the public
is what's most important.

657
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:50,666
Our townspeople deserve
a peaceful election.

658
00:36:51,500 --> 00:36:52,501
Thank you.

659
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:54,587
[crowd applauds]

660
00:37:05,431 --> 00:37:08,559
For a peaceful election!

661
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:10,311
[crowd applauds]

662
00:37:17,026 --> 00:37:19,278
[crowd chants] Diego! Diego! Diego!

663
00:37:20,529 --> 00:37:23,950
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

664
00:37:29,247 --> 00:37:31,874
Diego! Diego! Diego!

665
00:37:38,631 --> 00:37:39,590
Lily!

666
00:37:40,424 --> 00:37:41,634
Lily Cruz!

667
00:37:42,385 --> 00:37:43,678
Lily!

668
00:37:43,761 --> 00:37:45,638
You're such a snob!

669
00:37:46,764 --> 00:37:49,684
You know, Diego and Arnaldo
aren't the only ones

670
00:37:49,767 --> 00:37:51,477
who deserve attention today.

671
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:54,021
You do too! You're a comeback kid!

672
00:37:54,105 --> 00:37:56,315
Wait, hold on. Press! People!

673
00:37:56,399 --> 00:37:59,443
Press! Come, over here!

674
00:38:00,361 --> 00:38:02,613
Ladies and gentlemen, here's Lily Cruz!

675
00:38:03,572 --> 00:38:05,616
-Oh.
-[Emilia giggles]

676
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:07,785
You aren't used to being in the limelight?

677
00:38:09,453 --> 00:38:10,663
That's really sad.

678
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:15,459
Yes, I am Lily Cruz.

679
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:18,713
I've come back to Poblacion Ardiente

680
00:38:18,796 --> 00:38:19,964
for my mother.

681
00:38:20,047 --> 00:38:21,549
Do you plan on filing a lawsuit

682
00:38:21,632 --> 00:38:24,427
against the Ardientes
like your mother did?

683
00:38:28,389 --> 00:38:31,100
Yes, my mother already filed
a complaint against the Ardientes

684
00:38:31,183 --> 00:38:33,185
for what they did to my family.

685
00:38:33,686 --> 00:38:36,856
But the Ardientes twisted the truth.

686
00:38:36,939 --> 00:38:39,358
Now, we're being more careful
about planning our next moves.

687
00:38:39,442 --> 00:38:43,112
That's why for now, we will
allow the public to decide

688
00:38:43,195 --> 00:38:45,406
what the most appropriate
punishment is for the Ardientes.

689
00:38:45,489 --> 00:38:47,533
-Excuse us.
-Wow! Wait.

690
00:38:47,616 --> 00:38:48,909
Not so fast.

691
00:38:48,993 --> 00:38:51,662
Looks like you can't just
push Lily Cruz around.

692
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:53,122
Auntie, that's what you think.

693
00:38:53,205 --> 00:38:54,790
I'm not done with you yet.

694
00:38:54,874 --> 00:38:56,042
Hold on. Hold on.

695
00:38:57,793 --> 00:38:59,503
Mayor, can you grant us an interview?

696
00:38:59,587 --> 00:39:01,756
-Just a quick one.
-Of course, hon.

697
00:39:01,839 --> 00:39:02,882
Sure.

698
00:39:02,965 --> 00:39:04,884
Is it true your ratings dropped?

699
00:39:04,967 --> 00:39:07,595
Is that why you signed a peace
agreement with your brother?

700
00:39:08,721 --> 00:39:11,474
That's not true. In fact…

701
00:39:11,557 --> 00:39:15,478
Things are getting out of hand,
as I said earlier.

702
00:39:15,561 --> 00:39:18,814
We don't want innocent people
getting caught in this mess.

703
00:39:18,898 --> 00:39:23,444
That's why my brother and I
decided to settle things,

704
00:39:23,527 --> 00:39:26,238
so our town can be peaceful once again.

705
00:39:26,322 --> 00:39:29,325
Okay. What are your other plans
for this successful

706
00:39:29,408 --> 00:39:31,744
peaceful agreement
between you and your brother?

707
00:39:31,827 --> 00:39:33,162
[Arnaldo] Other plans than that?

708
00:39:33,245 --> 00:39:35,915
Well, I need to focus on my campaign.

709
00:39:43,964 --> 00:39:45,966
[slow tense music playing]

710
00:40:04,568 --> 00:40:05,611
Hey.

711
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:07,571
Do you have a new theme song?

712
00:40:08,239 --> 00:40:09,782
Do you want to record a whole album,

713
00:40:09,865 --> 00:40:11,534
so you can gaze lovingly at each other?

714
00:40:11,617 --> 00:40:13,035
[Diego] You have a lot of ideas.

715
00:40:13,244 --> 00:40:14,954
Why don't you run for president?

716
00:40:15,579 --> 00:40:16,622
You might end up winning.

717
00:40:17,039 --> 00:40:18,666
Arnaldo, what are you insinuating?

718
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:20,626
We are under one roof.

719
00:40:20,709 --> 00:40:22,837
First of all, yes, I will run
for president someday.

720
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:24,630
-Good for you.
-But for now…

721
00:40:25,506 --> 00:40:26,674
isn't the real Lily Cruz back?

722
00:40:26,757 --> 00:40:28,300
Why don't you stay close to her,

723
00:40:28,384 --> 00:40:29,510
instead of coming near Ivy?

724
00:40:29,593 --> 00:40:31,220
You don't need to tell me that.

725
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:34,640
Good.

726
00:40:34,723 --> 00:40:37,518
Can I trust you'll stay close
to Lily Cruz,

727
00:40:37,601 --> 00:40:39,145
instead of my fiancée from now on?

728
00:40:40,354 --> 00:40:41,397
Yes?

729
00:40:46,277 --> 00:40:47,653
Okay, I'll take that as a yes.

730
00:40:47,736 --> 00:40:49,155
Now, get out of my face.

731
00:40:50,573 --> 00:40:51,532
Hon.

732
00:41:03,627 --> 00:41:07,298
Hon, you just signed a peace agreement.

733
00:41:07,381 --> 00:41:09,633
Why are you getting all jealous again?

734
00:41:09,717 --> 00:41:11,719
I'm all yours.

735
00:41:11,802 --> 00:41:13,637
I'm yours, Arnaldo.

736
00:41:14,722 --> 00:41:15,764
Okay?

737
00:41:22,563 --> 00:41:24,148
Okay, okay.

738
00:41:30,779 --> 00:41:31,780
Auntie, Lily.

739
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:35,993
-Let's go.
-Do me a favor, Emilia.

740
00:41:36,452 --> 00:41:38,245
The next time you want to talk to me,

741
00:41:38,329 --> 00:41:41,790
just give it to me straight,
stop beating around the bush.

742
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:44,126
Let's stop wasting time, Emilia.

743
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:45,961
Okay. I won't waste your time.

744
00:41:46,045 --> 00:41:47,838
Can I have five minutes
of your precious time?

745
00:41:47,922 --> 00:41:49,757
Tell me the story of your life.

746
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,718
Why is it that after years
of being away from Ardiente,

747
00:41:52,801 --> 00:41:55,304
you suddenly come back, out of the blue,

748
00:41:55,387 --> 00:41:57,765
all poised and successful?

749
00:41:57,848 --> 00:41:59,600
Let me guess.

750
00:42:00,184 --> 00:42:03,020
Is this like a "rags to riches" story?

751
00:42:03,103 --> 00:42:05,940
Or like the ones I read in the books

752
00:42:06,023 --> 00:42:08,150
where the girl sells her body
in exchange for wealth?

753
00:42:08,234 --> 00:42:09,693
Don't be rude!

754
00:42:10,319 --> 00:42:11,612
[tense music playing]

755
00:42:12,571 --> 00:42:14,949
Then tell me the truth!
Who are you, really?

756
00:42:15,032 --> 00:42:16,700
Are you deaf, Emilia?

757
00:42:16,784 --> 00:42:20,412
How many times do I need
to tell you that I'm Lily Cruz?!

758
00:42:20,496 --> 00:42:23,207
I was orphaned, but I soldiered on.

759
00:42:23,290 --> 00:42:24,917
I got an education.

760
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:28,003
I found a good job,
that's why I have a decent life.

761
00:42:29,004 --> 00:42:31,215
I'm not an Ardiente like you.

762
00:42:31,298 --> 00:42:33,259
But that's actually a good thing

763
00:42:33,342 --> 00:42:35,427
because I actually pity you

764
00:42:35,511 --> 00:42:37,012
since that's all you have.

765
00:42:37,721 --> 00:42:39,473
And if you weren't an Ardiente,

766
00:42:39,557 --> 00:42:42,601
you'd be worse than a rotting fish
being swarmed by maggots.

767
00:42:42,685 --> 00:42:44,228
You better watch your tongue!

768
00:42:46,146 --> 00:42:48,023
First of all, you have no right

769
00:42:48,107 --> 00:42:49,858
to speak to my daughter that way!

770
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:53,487
Second, you have no right
to strike my daughter's face

771
00:42:53,571 --> 00:42:55,864
with that filthy hand of yours!

772
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:08,669
Both of you, please remember:

773
00:43:08,752 --> 00:43:10,212
I'm not done with you yet.

774
00:43:10,296 --> 00:43:11,839
You won't get away with this!

775
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:13,424
You will burn in hell!

776
00:43:13,507 --> 00:43:14,550
That's enough, Emilia!

777
00:43:17,678 --> 00:43:20,431
Your days of torturing Lily
and her family are over.

778
00:43:22,099 --> 00:43:23,058
Why, Diego?

779
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:26,770
Do you think that we're done
giving you a hard time?

780
00:43:26,854 --> 00:43:28,647
You're the only one here
who still believes

781
00:43:28,731 --> 00:43:30,566
we should be scared of you, Emilia.

782
00:43:30,941 --> 00:43:32,484
But the truth is,

783
00:43:32,568 --> 00:43:33,819
you're the one who's scared!

784
00:43:34,361 --> 00:43:36,530
Because the moment justice prevails,

785
00:43:36,864 --> 00:43:38,574
you'll get what you deserve.

786
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:41,702
Wow!

787
00:43:42,703 --> 00:43:44,204
I'm so scared.

788
00:43:44,747 --> 00:43:46,373
Can you believe that, Auntie?

789
00:43:46,457 --> 00:43:48,417
They had a lot to say. They talk too much!

790
00:43:48,500 --> 00:43:50,586
All I asked was if
she was Lily Cruz, right?

791
00:43:52,755 --> 00:43:54,757
-[Arnaldo] So, let's go?
-[Emilia] Let's go!

792
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:56,550
They're so irritating!

793
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:04,600
-Good morning, Congressman.
-Good morning.

794
00:44:12,775 --> 00:44:13,609
[grunts]

795
00:44:13,692 --> 00:44:14,526
Congressman.

796
00:44:14,610 --> 00:44:16,278
Don't touch me!

797
00:44:24,286 --> 00:44:26,288
[tense music playing]

798
00:44:35,297 --> 00:44:36,965
That was one of the Jaguar's men!

799
00:44:37,049 --> 00:44:38,634
He's here! The Jaguar's here!

800
00:44:38,717 --> 00:44:40,844
Where's Arnaldo?! Where is he?!

801
00:44:40,928 --> 00:44:42,554
-He's upstairs, Congressman.
-Get him!

802
00:44:42,638 --> 00:44:45,474
And get him out of
this building! Right now!

803
00:44:54,274 --> 00:44:55,901
Yes, you're right.

804
00:44:55,984 --> 00:44:57,569
The peace treaty was my idea.

805
00:44:58,487 --> 00:45:00,489
But, of course, that doesn't mean

806
00:45:00,572 --> 00:45:03,450
we'll really patch things up
with the Ardientes.

807
00:45:03,534 --> 00:45:05,327
That will never happen.

808
00:45:05,661 --> 00:45:09,498
Naturally, Anna, Emilia has
wanted to have you killed

809
00:45:09,581 --> 00:45:11,166
since you made the revelation.

810
00:45:11,708 --> 00:45:13,419
But that peace agreement

811
00:45:13,502 --> 00:45:16,004
is the only thing
stopping her from killing you.

812
00:45:16,672 --> 00:45:18,966
Ivy, we know the Ardientes well.

813
00:45:19,425 --> 00:45:20,843
They don't keep their word.

814
00:45:20,926 --> 00:45:23,554
They're just going with
this peace treaty agreement.

815
00:45:23,637 --> 00:45:25,806
We shouldn't let our guard down.

816
00:45:25,889 --> 00:45:27,975
Leave the security
of the headquarters to me.

817
00:45:28,058 --> 00:45:30,477
I'll teach the volunteers
that Mister Pandoy brought in.

818
00:45:30,561 --> 00:45:32,896
[Diego] We can't let them have
the advantage over us.

819
00:45:32,980 --> 00:45:34,648
I'll work harder on the campaign,

820
00:45:34,731 --> 00:45:36,984
and I'll make sure that we win.

821
00:45:37,568 --> 00:45:39,570
Do what you need to do.

822
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:41,321
Anna.

823
00:45:42,656 --> 00:45:44,116
Were you all right back there?

824
00:45:47,578 --> 00:45:48,996
I already told you

825
00:45:49,079 --> 00:45:51,039
you're getting yourself
into something serious.

826
00:45:53,333 --> 00:45:54,251
You'll need this.

827
00:45:54,334 --> 00:45:57,546
Jepoy, you will teach Anna
how to use this.

828
00:46:00,174 --> 00:46:01,633
You need that gun.

829
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:04,136
You need to protect yourself.

830
00:46:06,013 --> 00:46:07,181
Diego and Jepoy…

831
00:46:09,766 --> 00:46:11,643
I want you two to protect Anna.

832
00:46:12,603 --> 00:46:14,062
She's important to me.

833
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:17,232
So, she should never be harmed by anyone.

834
00:46:19,109 --> 00:46:20,235
You can count on us.

835
00:46:23,572 --> 00:46:24,531
How about you, Ivy?

836
00:46:25,032 --> 00:46:26,700
After everything that happened,

837
00:46:27,701 --> 00:46:29,578
are you still marrying Arnaldo?

838
00:46:30,579 --> 00:46:31,497
Yes.

839
00:46:36,919 --> 00:46:38,879
The wedding must push through.

840
00:46:40,464 --> 00:46:42,841
It needs to push through.

841
00:46:57,147 --> 00:47:00,526
<i>I would like you to take care</i>
<i>of one of our enemies.</i>

842
00:47:00,609 --> 00:47:04,279
<i>Kill Jaguar for the sake of our family.</i>

843
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:05,322
<i>Ping!</i>

844
00:47:05,405 --> 00:47:06,365
<i>Thank you for coming here today</i>

845
00:47:06,448 --> 00:47:09,535
<i>for the Poblacion Ardiente public debate.</i>

846
00:47:09,618 --> 00:47:11,995
<i>You haven't been in</i>
<i>any government position before.</i>

847
00:47:12,079 --> 00:47:15,207
<i>Wouldn't it be better if our lives</i>
<i>all improved together?</i>

848
00:47:15,290 --> 00:47:16,750
<i>You're running out of time, Mayor.</i>

849
00:47:18,418 --> 00:47:19,503
<i>Mayor?</i>

850
00:47:19,586 --> 00:47:23,006
[Ivy] <i>I think it's time</i>
<i>the public found out</i>

851
00:47:23,090 --> 00:47:26,009
<i>that my future husband</i>
<i>is going through something.</i>

852
00:47:26,093 --> 00:47:27,177
<i>What do you mean?</i>

853
00:47:27,261 --> 00:47:28,720
<i>Is the Mayor sick?</i>

854
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:32,432
[tense music playing]
